        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Melonball\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/m/46a35a/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Melonball:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Tempest is great, but the reason I dig the visionary/tachyon/legacy combo is synergy.&nbsp;visionary uses her power to feed tachyon cards and fuel her trash pile, legacy pumps damage so tachyons burst damage wrecks people, and all 3 of the decks deny damage and control the environment.&nbsp;as for voss, 2 gene bound guards at jump is a horror show.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Two damange reduction is nasty, for sure, but when you've got heroes that can fairly regularly beat it, particularly when boosted by Legacy, it's not as big of a deal. That's why the visionary/tachyon/legacy team looks so strange to me. I'm not saying it's not great! Just that I'm used to thinking in terms of being able to dish out regular amounts of at least medium-sized damage (3-5).</p>",
        "post_number": 7,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:26:14.504Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
